dditional ring routes, expanding its proposed network from seven to nine. These new corridors will cover approximately 307 km and will connect existing roads and planned projects across Mumbai, Thane, and Navi Mumbai.\n\n#### Thane Infrastructure and Development Updates\n\nThe Thane-Borivali Twin Tunnel project saw the launch of TBM Arjuna on August 13, 2026, aiming to reduce travel time between Thane and Borivali to approximately 15 minutes. Amazon Data Services is developing a large data center in Ambernath, with an estimated construction cost of ₹3,500 crore, to be ready by 2029\n\n#### Mumbai Boosts Connectivity with Santacruz - Chembur link road Phase 2 & Chembur Metro Station\n\nCM Devendra Fadnavis inaugurated Phase 2 of the Santacruz-Chembur Link Road (SCLR) & the Chembur Metro Station under Metro Line 2B,The SCLR Phase 2 is expected to strengthen the road network between Mumbai's western and eastern suburbs, improving east-west connectivity.\n\n#### Thane-Borivali Twin Tunnel Project: Traffic Diversions Announced in Kasarvadavali\n\nTemporary traffic diversions have been implemented in Kasarvadavali for the ongoing work on the ambitious Thane-Borivali twin tunnel project by the Mumbai Metropolitan Region Development Authority (MMRDA). Certain routes will be closed from July 6 to August 5, 2026, to facilitate construction.\n\n#### Mumbai Monorail Services to Resume After Nine-Month Hiatus\n\nMumbai's monorail services are set to resume soon after a nine-month suspension, following approval from the Maharashtra government for safety improvements and fare revisions. MMRDA has proposed increased ticket prices. The monorail, which previously carried around 18,000 passengers daily, will offer improved services after safety upgrades.\n\nRent in The Wadhwa Aquaria Grande ranges from ₹ 29 K to ₹ 3 L with options available for 1 BHK, 4 BHK.\n\n#### MMRDA Presents Surplus Budget with Significant Allocation for Infrastructure\n\nMMRDA has presented a surplus budget of ₹48,072 crore, with 87% allocated to infrastructure projects, including roads, public transport, and urban development. A notable provision of ₹4,000 crore is earmarked for the development of Mumbai 3.0 New Town, aiming for planned urban expansion.\n\n#### BMC Budget Includes ₹6,475 Crore for Water Security Projects\n\nThe BMC's FY26-27 budget includes a substantial allocation of ₹6,475 crore for water security initiatives. This funding is designated for projects such as the Manori desalination plant (₹500 crore) and the Gargai project (₹437.51 crore), aimed at augmenting the city's water supply capacity.\n\n#### BMC Budget Includes ₹6,475 Crore for Water Security Projects\n\nThe BMC's FY26-27 budget includes a substantial allocation of ₹6,475 crore for water security initiatives. This funding is designated for projects such as the Manori desalination plant (₹500 crore) and the Gargai project (₹437.51 crore), aimed at augmenting the city's water supply capacity.\n\n### Govt. Registrations\n\n2 Sales Transactions Registered in The Wadhwa Aquaria Grande From Oct 25 to Sep 26 at Avg. Price ₹ 16.6 K/Sq.Ft.\n\n| Sales Transactions | Gross Sales Value | Registered Rate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2 | ₹ 24 Cr | ₹ 16,650 / Sq. Ft. |\n\nTransaction Period Oct 25 to Sep 26\n\n## The Wadhwa Aquaria Grande Floor Plans\n\nThe 3, 4 BHK Flats at The Wadhwa Aquaria Grande are priced from ₹ 3.55 Cr to ₹ 4.98 Cr. 3 BHK: ₹ 3.55 Cr, 4 BHK: ₹ 4.73 Cr provides a detailed breakdown of costs for each configuration. The 4 different configurations offer a range of choices to suit varying needs\n\nThe Oil Bound Distemper, Vitrified Tiles, Premium Bath Fittings, RCC Frame Structure include information about the included amenities. The 1638 Sq.Ft. and 2297 Sq.Ft. of the apartments provide flexible options. Comparatively, the ₹ 35,900 /Sq.Ft. in the surrounding area gives context to the value proposition. Consider that the average asking price of ₹ 31,300 /Sq.Ft. in Borivali West.\n\n![Floor plan 